<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <PackageId>DeepSharp.Verso.Notebooks</PackageId>
    <Description>A DeepSharp pipeline written as a notebook in Verso, one block per step. The first block reads a comma-separated file, a Parquet file, a sheet of an Excel workbook or a JSON file, and the package brings those readers with it. Each block is the step's own JSON, edited as text or in Verso's properties panel, and shows the data at that point on request: a grid coloured per column over the training rows, a profile that names what should not be there and how each is answered, with a box that gives an answer which changes the columns, and a heatmap of the complete training rows. Columns are chosen from the grid or from a list of the source's columns, which says what each column's cells propose it holds, and the decisions are saved beside the notebook and taken over again. The notebook is the declaration — exported as the same pipeline file, and handed to C# cells as text. It runs in Verso's VS Code extension, in verso serve, in DeepSharp's own server deepsharp-serve and in an application of your own.</Description>
    <PackageTags>deepsharp;pipeline;pdd;machine-learning;data-preparation;verso;notebook;dotnet</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The oldest abstractions carrying every member this package calls: a cell type that keeps no outputs,
         an interaction that says it changed the notebook and sees the notebook's cells. Verso refuses an
         extension compiled against a newer minor than the one it runs, so the floor stays low and a test pins
         the version compiled against. A range rather than an exact pin: an exact pin beside Verso's own engine
         in one test project is NU1608, an error here (measured). -->
    <PackageReference Include="Verso.Abstractions" Version="[1.1.0, 2.0.0)" />
    <!-- The colour maps and the correlation are borrowed, as the indicators are; every figure is DeepSharp.Charts'. -->
    <PackageReference Include="MatPlotLibNet" Version="1.18.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DeepSharp.Charts\DeepSharp.Charts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DeepSharp.Pipelines\DeepSharp.Pipelines.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Indicators\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Indicators.csproj" />
    <!-- The readers a first block can name, carried as the indicators are: an extension Verso installs is loaded apart, so the notebook's verbs are only what this package brings. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Parquet\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Parquet.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Excel\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Excel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Json\DeepSharp.Pipelines.Json.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The session's parts are internal, and the suite measures what only they can say: how many times a source
         was parsed, which is the whole point of keeping one. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DeepSharp.Verso.Notebooks.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\assets\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
